(BUGS_FOUND #49/#104: `append each part from sink to out.` used to be
 refused - a buffer walked as a list misread its own header as a list's
 (bug #49), so the walk was rejected outright (formerly pinned by
 compile_fail/097). The byte-iteration sentence (#104) gives the walk a
 real meaning instead: `append each ... from <buffer> to <list>` reads
 each byte's value, so `out` ends up holding the byte values, not the
 old silently-misread header.)

a buffer called sink is "abc".
a list called out is [].
append each part from sink to out.
print out.
